{
  "_comment": [
    "The second dream-audience: the ghost, back, saying what it actually wanted.",
    "",
    "WORLD.md locks the dream-audiences as the relationship channel and as 'rage, then",
    "bargaining, then the discovery that the ghost NEEDS its killer'. The first dream was",
    "the bargaining, dressed as an estate handover. This is where the need surfaces, and",
    "it surfaces as the smallest possible ask: the god cannot see its own estate any more",
    "and would like to be told what the world is doing.",
    "",
    "It is gated on ENFORCEMENT, so the player has met a Warden. That is why the Wardens",
    "are what the god talks about: it wrote the policy they are still enforcing and it",
    "cannot amend it, because amending an order requires being alive. The rage in this",
    "scene is not aimed at the killer at any point. That is deliberate -- a ghost that",
    "shouted at the player would be a boss, and this is a bereavement.",
    "",
    "Dread covenant: the grief is sincere and is never the punchline. What is allowed to",
    "be funny is the administrative register and the god's pettiness about small things.",
    "The ghost never quips about the dying.",
    "",
    "TEXT VARIANTS on the opening, gated on THE_GHOST: how the first dream went is not",
    "stored as a flag, it is stored as regard, and the ghost's tone reading it back is",
    "the whole reason regard is bands rather than a boolean. Somebody who was cruel in",
    "the first dream gets a colder room. Nothing is HIDDEN by standing here -- only the",
    "wording moves -- because a player who timed out of the first dream holds no record",
    "at all, and an option they cannot see would be a dead end rather than a scene.",
    "",
    "Note again: no number for the family, and no explanation of 'Executor'."
  ],
